From: vllm-xpu-nix <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: reduce kernel-build peak memory

Cuts the peak compile-/link-time RAM of the SYCL kernel libraries
(attn_kernels_xe_2 and friends), which otherwise pushes 24-core builders
into swap or OOM.

  * `-fsycl-device-code-split=per_source` on every per-TU compile so each
    source's device IR stays an independent module instead of getting
    merged by the default `auto` heuristic. Shrinks the inputs the AOT
    backend (spirv-translator + ocloc) processes at link time.

  * `-fsycl-max-parallel-link-jobs` becomes a CMake cache var
    (`VLLM_XPU_SYCL_LINK_PARALLELISM`, default 4) instead of being
    hardcoded at 16. Device link is the memory peak: every inner job
    holds the full fat-module bitcode plus its own LLVM context plus the
    AOT backend, and up to four kernel libraries link concurrently, so
    16 inner jobs is far more aggressive than typical hardware can
    absorb. Override at configure time to raise on memory-rich machines.

  * `-ftemplate-backtrace-limit=10` (was 0/unlimited) and
    `-fno-pretty-templates` on the CUTLASS-SYCL TUs. The unlimited
    backtrace makes the frontend retain the entire template
    instantiation chain for diagnostics that almost never fire;
    CUTLASS-SYCL is template-pathological and pays this cost across
    ~200 TUs. Real errors still get a 10-frame trace; devs debugging
    deeper template chains can override locally.

`-flink-huge-device-code` is intentionally left in place — at this
kernel scale the device linker truncates relocations without it.
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -197,6 +197,7 @@

   set(SYCL_COMPILE_FLAGS ${SYCL_FLAGS})
   set(SYCL_COMPILE_FLAGS ${SYCL_COMPILE_FLAGS} "-O3" "-DNDEBUG")
+  set(SYCL_COMPILE_FLAGS ${SYCL_COMPILE_FLAGS} "-fsycl-device-code-split=per_source")
   if(AOT_DEVICES)
     set(SYCL_COMPILE_FLAGS ${SYCL_COMPILE_FLAGS} -fsycl-targets=spir64_gen)
   endif()
@@ -206,11 +207,14 @@
   set(VLLM_GPU_COMPILE_FLAGS ${SYCL_COMPILE_FLAGS})

   # ============= LINK OPTIONS ==================
+  set(VLLM_XPU_SYCL_LINK_PARALLELISM "4" CACHE STRING
+      "Inner parallelism for SYCL device link (-fsycl-max-parallel-link-jobs). Lower values reduce peak link-time memory.")
   set(SYCL_LINK_FLAGS "")
   list(APPEND SYCL_LINK_FLAGS "-fsycl")
   set(SYCL_DEVICE_LINK_FLAGS ${SYCL_LINK_FLAGS})
   set(SYCL_DEVICE_LINK_FLAGS
-      ${SYCL_DEVICE_LINK_FLAGS} -fsycl-max-parallel-link-jobs=16
+      ${SYCL_DEVICE_LINK_FLAGS}
+      -fsycl-max-parallel-link-jobs=${VLLM_XPU_SYCL_LINK_PARALLELISM}
       -flink-huge-device-code)
   set(SYCL_DEVICE_LINK_FLAGS
       ${SYCL_DEVICE_LINK_FLAGS}
@@ -314,7 +318,8 @@
   list(APPEND VLLM_CUTLASS_FLAGS "-DCUTLASS_ENABLE_SYCL")
   list(APPEND VLLM_CUTLASS_FLAGS "-DSYCL_INTEL_TARGET")
   list(APPEND VLLM_CUTLASS_FLAGS "-DCUTLASS_VERSIONS_GENERATED")
-  list(APPEND VLLM_CUTLASS_FLAGS "-ftemplate-backtrace-limit=0")
+  list(APPEND VLLM_CUTLASS_FLAGS "-ftemplate-backtrace-limit=10")
+  list(APPEND VLLM_CUTLASS_FLAGS "-fno-pretty-templates")
   list(APPEND VLLM_CUTLASS_FLAGS "-fdiagnostics-color=always")
 endif()

